              <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            </button>
          </h2>
          <div class="details" id="faq-panel-1">
            <p>Cats purr for many reasons — contentment, self-soothing, and healing. The frequency of a cat's purr (between 25 and 150 Hertz) has been shown to improve bone density and promote healing in both cats and humans.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="example">
          <h2>
            <button type="button" aria-expanded="false" class="faq-trigger" id="faq-trigger-2" aria-controls="faq-panel-2">
              Why do cats knead (make biscuits)?
              <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            </button>
          </h2>
          <div class="details" id="faq-panel-2">
            <p>Kneading is a behavior carried over from kittenhood. Kittens knead their mothers to stimulate milk flow. As adults, they often do it when they feel safe, comfortable, and happy.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="example">
          <h2>
            <button type="button" aria-expanded="false" class="faq-trigger" id="faq-trigger-3" aria-controls="faq-panel-3">
